<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7470" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēpheus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissyl.</span></b> ), ei (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i>
			Cēphĕos, Germ. Arat. 189; acc.
			Cēphĕă, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
			42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 11, 3</span></i>), m., =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κηφεύς</span>, <i>a king
				of Ethiopia</i> (acc. to Mel. l. l. at Joppa, in Phoenicia),
				<i>husband of Cassiope. father of Andromeda</i>,
				<i>and father-in-law of Perseus;</i> finally
			placed with these three among the stars, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
				738</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Astr. 2, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				5, 3, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. N. D. 2, 43, 111</span></i>; Germ. Arat.
			184 al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, <i>adjj.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphēïus</span></b> , a, um,
				<i>of Cepheus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andromeda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 3, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 15, 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgo, the same,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A. 3, 3, 17</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphēus</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ),
				a, um, <i>of Cepheus</i>, = <i>Ethiopian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Meroe,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 6, 78: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 669</span></i>
			.  —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphēïs</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f., = <i>Andromeda</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 3, 191</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Manil. 1, 426</span></i>.</div>
